	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/video_settings/first_person/help_strings">
		<string text=""/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="How wide your weapon and hands are drawn, in degrees across a 16:9 screen: wider draws them smaller. Default keeps the weapon's own view.|Click the number (or press A) to type any from 20 to 150."/>
		<string text="Moves your weapon and hands right, or left below 0, in centimeters, for every weapon, as far on the screen at any weapon field of view. 0 keeps them where the game puts them.|Click the number (or press A) to type any from -20 to 20."/>
		<string text="Moves your weapon and hands up, or down below 0, in centimeters. Lower it to see more of the screen.|Click the number (or press A) to type any from -20 to 20."/>
		<string text="Pushes your weapon and hands away from you, or closer below 0, in centimeters. Too close and they cut off.|Click the number (or press A) to type any from -20 to 20."/>
		<string text="How wide you see in a vehicle, in degrees across a 16:9 screen. Default keeps the game's view; Match uses your Field of View.|Click the number (or press A) to type any from 20 to 150."/>
		<string text="Stops a wide field of view from stretching what is at the sides; you still see as far, and the middle is drawn larger. 1 keeps their shapes true. The HUD stays flat.|Click the number (or press A) to type 0 to 1."/>
		<string text="With Panini Projection on: straightens floors and ceilings above and below the middle, and stretches the sides taller. 0 keeps their shapes true.|Click the number (or press A) to type 0 to 1."/>
		<string text="Puts the reticle below the middle of the screen, as Halo 2 and 3 do. Your view tilts up a little, so shots still go where the reticle points. Zooming centers it."/>
		<string text="How far below the middle the lowered reticle sits, in percent of the screen's height. 10 is about Halo 2's and 3's.|Click the number (or press A) to type any from 0 to 30."/>
		<string text="Draws your weapon, your hands and what they hold. Hide clears the view; you still fire, reload and hear them."/>
		<string text="Your legs when you look down, moving as you run: your body as the others see it."/>
		<string text="Riding in a Warthog or a Scorpion in the campaign and co-op: the view from behind the vehicle, or from your seat. Behind, the weapon cannot zoom."/>
		<string text="Your shield's flare on your first-person arms, its color, and an overshield's glow."/>
	</strings>
